Scanners generated by flex 2.6.5 define _POSIX_C_SOURCE and _POSIX_SOURCE
to 1 when no feature test macro has been set, so that fileno() is declared
when compiling in a strict ISO C mode. This is done after <assert.h> has
been included, on the assumption that the C library will have set its
default feature test macros by then, which makes the block a no-op with
glibc.

illumos does not define _POSIX_C_SOURCE by default, so there the block
takes effect and restricts the namespace of every header that is included
afterwards. Types such as siginfo_t and label_t are no longer visible to
the code in the scanner's own prologue, which breaks existing consumers.

Skip the block on illumos, where fileno() is visible in the default
compilation environment. This restores the behaviour of flex 2.6.4.

diff -wpruN --no-dereference '--exclude=*.orig' a~/src/c99-flex.skl a/src/c99-flex.skl
--- a~/src/c99-flex.skl	1970-01-01 00:00:00
+++ a/src/c99-flex.skl	1970-01-01 00:00:00
@@ -228,7 +228,7 @@ m4_ifdef( [[M4_YY_ALWAYS_INTERACTIVE]],
 #include <assert.h>
 #endif
 #if !(defined(_POSIX_C_SOURCE) || defined(_XOPEN_SOURCE) || \
-    defined(_POSIX_SOURCE))
+    defined(_POSIX_SOURCE) || defined(__illumos__))
 # define _POSIX_C_SOURCE 1 /* Required for fileno() */
 # define _POSIX_SOURCE 1
 #endif]])]])
